# PulseForge

PulseForge is a lightweight API availability and latency monitor built with Go.

It provides a simple CLI for checking HTTP endpoints and returning structured
results that can be consumed by scripts, CI pipelines, monitoring systems,
and automation workflows.

## Features

- HTTP endpoint health checks
- Configurable request timeout
- Latency measurement
- HTTP status inspection
- JSON output for automation
- Minimal dependencies
- Fast startup
- CI/CD friendly
- Non-zero exit codes for failed checks

## Installation

Clone the repository:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/yourusername/pulseforge.git
cd pulseforge
go build -o pulseforge ./cmd/pulseforge
./pulseforge --url https://example.com
./pulseforge \
  --url https://example.com \
  --timeout 5s
./pulseforge \
  --url https://example.com \
  --json
{
  "url": "https://example.com",
  "status_code": 200,
  "latency": 142310000,
  "available": true,
  "timestamp": "2026-09-07T11:10:24Z"
}
